From: Eduard Ryzhov <1711255+ryzed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd9335: start the SLIMbus RX stream once the
 DAC is up

Replaces the earlier 0014 ("enable the SLIMbus stream from hw_params").

The msm8976 ADSP (MSM8956/MSM8976, Xiaomi Redmi Note 3 Pro "kenzo") refuses
AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START for a SLIMbus port while the shared channels it names
are not active, so the channels must be up before the AFE port starts
(q6afe-dai, patch 0016, starts it after trigger()).

Playback: an RX port bound to an active channel before the interpolator behind
it runs overflows at once and never recovers - PORT_INT_STATUS 0x82,
"overflow error on RX port 0", silence.  Every variant that enabled the port
from hw_params() or from the AIF widget did so, because DAPM powers aif_in
before the interpolator.  Android (tasha_codec_enable_slimrx ->
wcd9xxx_cfg_slim_sch_rx) programs the port, connects it and activates the
channel only after the interpolator, mix path and DAC are powered; Fairphone 3
(mainline) activates the channel from the codec trigger(), after DAPM.  Here the
RX stream is started from the DAC PRE_PMU events (EAR, HPHL/HPHR, LINEOUT1-4):
the interpolator already runs, the AFE port has not started yet.  With this the
port reads 0x21 during playback, like Android, and the speaker plays.

Stop: the channels stay up across STOP, pause and a restart without hw_free()
(XRUN, resume), like the AFE port, and are removed from hw_free(), after the CPU
DAI's hw_free() has stopped the AFE port - the order Android uses (AFE close,
then channel removal).  For playback the AFE port is the source, and removing
the channels under a running AFE port crashed the DSP and rebooted the SoC.
Nothing waits for the bus or the DSP from trigger() any more.  The RX port
registers are left programmed on stop, as Android does: the channel is removed
and the port disconnected, PORT_INT_STATUS drops to 0x00; clearing them before
the disconnect left the port bound (0x21) and made the next start overflow.
A new prepare() starts the RX stream when hw_free()/hw_params() ran on an open
stream whose path stays powered.

Capture: the TX stream is still enabled from hw_params(), before the AFE port.

Also: free the stream runtime and the channel list in hw_free() and before a
repeated hw_params() (they leaked), and drop kfree(sconfig.chs) from the AIF
POST_PMD handler - the buffer belongs to hw_params()/hw_free(), and freeing it
there without clearing the pointer was a double free.

Tested on kenzo (09.11.2026, with 0016 and 0017): speaker tones back to back,
an XRUN restart in the middle of a stream, playback and capture at the same
time (a 1500 Hz tone recorded as 1500.04 Hz); no overflow, no reboot on stop,
PORT_INT_STATUS 0x21 during playback and 0x00 after, as on Android.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
